======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  MMH23 showed AeST departs from MOND at KiDS radii unless m^2 <~ 1e-3 - 1 Mpc^-2 AND each galaxy's boundary constant C is tuned, and
  said no mechanism was known to set C.  The matching theorem is the mechanism: the well's charge is the conserved shift charge that
  fell in.  With C fixed that way, AeST is excluded on the KiDS-1000 isolated rail at Delta chi2 >= +100 for every m^2 from 1e-4 to
  100 Mpc^-2 and both a_0 footings, at the external fields isolated galaxies actually sit in (0.03-0.1 a_0).  For the m^2 MMH23's
  lensing horn allows, the charge cannot even sit in quasistatic equilibrium (C - Phi(0) >= 10 well depths): it is a pile-up, and
  the mass count is what lensing sees.  Both ways: an external field of order 0.3 a_0, unphysical for isolated lenses, throttles the
  accretion into the +/-0.3 dex amplitude budget.  Closure of AeST at galaxy-lensing scales given (a) the accretion estimate (spherical
  collapse, EFE, no N-body of AeST exists) and (b) the +/-0.3 dex amplitude budget; horn 1 is MMH23's, horn 2 is this programme's.

